    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN output confirms a heap-buffer-overflow READ at `gthreadedresolver.c:714` in `g_resolver_records_from_res_query`, exactly at the `GETSHORT(type, p)` call — reading 1 byte past the end of the 13-byte buffer.\n\nThe crash matches the reported issue: a heap-buffer-overflow in `fuzz_resolver` caused by insufficient length validation before parsing DNS response data. The root cause is that `g_resolver_records_from_res_query` only checks `len > 0` but doesn't verify the buffer is large enough for the HEADER struct or the subsequent record parsing fields.",
